# "You may play lands from your graveyard" (CR 305.1): Bot1 sacrifices Marsh Flats on turn 1 and casts Ancient
# Greenwarden. On turn 3 it plays a Forest from its hand instead of the Marsh Flats (declining) and casts Sazh's
# Chocobo; on turn 5 it plays the Marsh Flats from its own graveyard (accepting) and the Chocobo's landfall triggers
# twice for the land entering. Bot2's Marsh Flats in Bot2's graveyard stays there - the permission is its controller's
# alone - and it does not let a land card's own ability be activated from a graveyard (CR 602.2a).

